{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useHotkeySequences(definitions, commonOptions?): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequences.ts#L68","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHotkeySequences.ts:68"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue composable for registering multiple keyboard shortcut sequences at once (Vim-style)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses the singleton SequenceManager. Accepts a dynamic array of definitions, or a getter/ref\nthat returns one, so you can register variable-length lists safely."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options are merged in this order:\nHotkeysProvider defaults < commonOptions < per-definition options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definitions with an empty "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sequence"},{"type":"text","value":" are skipped (no registration)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"definitions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeRefOrGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceDefinition.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseHotkeySequenceDefinition"}]},{"type":"text","value":"[]>"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array of sequence definitions, or a getter/ref"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"commonoptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"commonOptions?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MaybeRefOrGetter"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseHotkeySequenceOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared options applied to all sequences (overridden by per-definition options)"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { useHotkeySequences } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nuseHotkeySequences([\n  { sequence: ['G', 'G'], callback: () => scrollToTop() },\n  { sequence: ['D', 'D'], callback: () => deleteLine() },\n])\n</script>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup>\nimport { computed } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkeySequences } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst items = computed(() => [...])\nuseHotkeySequences(\n  () => items.value.map((item) => ({\n    sequence: item.chords,\n    callback: item.action,\n    options: { enabled: item.enabled },\n  })),\n  { preventDefault: true },\n)\n</script>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"definitions","text":"definitions","level":3},{"id":"commonoptions","text":"commonOptions?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeySequences(definitions, commonOptions?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeySequences.ts:68](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequences.ts#L68)\n\nVue composable for registering multiple keyboard shortcut sequences at once (Vim-style).\n\nUses the singleton SequenceManager. Accepts a dynamic array of definitions, or a getter/ref\nthat returns one, so you can register variable-length lists safely.\n\nOptions are merged in this order:\nHotkeysProvider defaults < commonOptions < per-definition options\n\nDefinitions with an empty `sequence` are skipped (no registration).\n\n## Parameters\n\n### definitions\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeySequenceDefinition`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceDefinition.md)[]\\>\n\nArray of sequence definitions, or a getter/ref\n\n### commonOptions?\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\nShared options applied to all sequences (overridden by per-definition options)\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useHotkeySequences } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nuseHotkeySequences([\n  { sequence: ['G', 'G'], callback: () => scrollToTop() },\n  { sequence: ['D', 'D'], callback: () => deleteLine() },\n])\n</script>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { computed } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkeySequences } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst items = computed(() => [...])\nuseHotkeySequences(\n  () => items.value.map((item) => ({\n    sequence: item.chords,\n    callback: item.action,\n    options: { enabled: item.enabled },\n  })),\n  { preventDefault: true },\n)\n</script>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHotkeySequences\ntitle: useHotkeySequences\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeySequences(definitions, commonOptions?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeySequences.ts:68](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/vue-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequences.ts#L68)\n\nVue composable for registering multiple keyboard shortcut sequences at once (Vim-style).\n\nUses the singleton SequenceManager. Accepts a dynamic array of definitions, or a getter/ref\nthat returns one, so you can register variable-length lists safely.\n\nOptions are merged in this order:\nHotkeysProvider defaults < commonOptions < per-definition options\n\nDefinitions with an empty `sequence` are skipped (no registration).\n\n## Parameters\n\n### definitions\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeySequenceDefinition`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceDefinition.md)[]\\>\n\nArray of sequence definitions, or a getter/ref\n\n### commonOptions?\n\n`MaybeRefOrGetter`\\<[`UseHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md)\\> = `{}`\n\nShared options applied to all sequences (overridden by per-definition options)\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Examples\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { useHotkeySequences } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nuseHotkeySequences([\n  { sequence: ['G', 'G'], callback: () => scrollToTop() },\n  { sequence: ['D', 'D'], callback: () => deleteLine() },\n])\n</script>\n```\n\n```vue\n<script setup>\nimport { computed } from 'vue'\nimport { useHotkeySequences } from '@tanstack/vue-hotkeys'\n\nconst items = computed(() => [...])\nuseHotkeySequences(\n  () => items.value.map((item) => ({\n    sequence: item.chords,\n    callback: item.action,\n    options: { enabled: item.enabled },\n  })),\n  { preventDefault: true },\n)\n</script>\n```\n"}
